{"type":"tool/result","data":{"turn":1,"step":1,"message":{"source":{"kind":"tool","callId":"load-ponytail-help"},"content":[{"type":"tool-result","toolCallId":"load-ponytail-help","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<skill_content name=\\"ponytail-help\\">\\n<skill_resources>\\nBase directory for this skill: {{skillRoot}}/ponytail-help\\nResolve relative paths mentioned by this skill against the base directory before using them. Load referenced resources only as needed.\\n</skill_resources>\\n\\n<skill_instructions>\\n## arx Harness integration\\n\\nThese are model-independent instructions, not a Claude Code plugin. Use the arx \`skill\` tool or explicit \`/ponytail-help\` invocation; do not run marketplace installers, hooks, auto-updaters, or write mode flags. Availability requires the session to expose the \`skill\` tool. Follow the repository instructions, requested scope, approval policy, security requirements, documentation obligations, and existing test framework. Never remove required validation or tests to reduce line count. Guidance remains ordinary logged context until compaction; no automatic activation, durable intensity setting, or child-context propagation is installed. For other capabilities, keep consulting the existing skills-globais catalog.\\n\\n# Ponytail Help\\n\\n| Skill | Purpose |\\n|---|---|\\n| ponytail | Reuse existing code, standard libraries, and platform features before adding code. |\\n| ponytail-review | Review a diff for unnecessary complexity; apply nothing. |\\n| ponytail-audit | Audit a requested repository scope for complexity; apply nothing. |\\n| ponytail-debt | Report explicit \`ponytail:\` deferral comments. |\\n| ponytail-gain | Explain upstream benchmark evidence and limits. |\\n| ponytail-help | Show this reference. |\\n\\nInvoke \`/ponytail\`, \`/ponytail-review\`, or another exact skill name, or ask the agent to load that skill. Request lite (suggest alternatives), full (prefer the smallest valid implementation), or ultra (challenge speculative additions) in ordinary task text. Explicit user requirements and repository checks remain mandatory at every intensity. Say \\"stop ponytail\\" or \\"normal mode\\" to end the guidance.\\n\\nAll configured model routes can access these skills when the session exposes the arx \`skill\` tool; no Claude account or native plugin installer is required. The minimal preset does not expose that tool. There is no automatic session mode, environment-variable mode selector, status line, or automatic update. Compaction or an independent child can require another skill load. Updates are reviewed source changes pinned in the integration provenance, not \`/plugin\` commands. This help changes no configuration.\\n</skill_instructions>\\n</skill_content>"}],"isError":false}],"role":"user","id":"{{sessionId}}"}},"sourceEventSeqs":[36],"surfaceOp":"append"}
{"type":"tool/call","data":{"turn":1,"step":1,"callId":"load-ponytail-review","name":"skill","arguments":"{\\"name\\":\\"ponytail-review\\"}"}}
{"type":"tool/result","data":{"turn":1,"step":1,"message":{"source":{"kind":"tool","callId":"load-ponytail-review"},"content":[{"type":"tool-result","toolCallId":"load-ponytail-review","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<skill_content name=\\"ponytail-review\\">\\n<skill_resources>\\nBase directory for this skill: {{skillRoot}}/ponytail-review\\nResolve relative paths mentioned by this skill against the base directory before using them. Load referenced resources only as needed.\\n</skill_resources>\\n\\n<skill_instructions>\\n## arx Harness integration\\n\\nThese are model-independent instructions, not a Claude Code plugin. Use the arx \`skill\` tool or explicit \`/ponytail-review\` invocation; do not run marketplace installers, hooks, auto-updaters, or write mode flags. Availability requires the session to expose the \`skill\` tool. Follow the repository instructions, requested scope, approval policy, security requirements, documentation obligations, and existing test framework. Never remove required validation or tests to reduce line count. Guidance remains ordinary logged context until compaction; no automatic activation, durable intensity setting, or child-context propagation is installed. For other capabilities, keep consulting the existing skills-globais catalog.\\n\\n\\nReview diffs for unnecessary complexity. One line per finding: location, what to cut, what replaces it. The diff's best outcome is getting shorter.\\n\\n## Format\\n\\n\`L<line>: <tag> <what>. <replacement>.\`, or \`<file>:L<line>: ...\` for multi-file diffs.\\n\\nTags:\\n\\n- \`delete:\` dead code, unused flexibility, speculative feature. Replacement: nothing.\\n- \`stdlib:\` hand-rolled thing the standard library ships. Name the function.\\n- \`native:\` dependency or code doing what the platform already does. Name the feature.\\n- \`reuse:\` equivalent helper, util, or pattern already in this repo. Name the path.\\n- \`yagni:\` abstraction with one implementation, config nobody sets, layer with one caller.\\n- \`shrink:\` same logic, fewer lines. Show the shorter form.\\n\\n\\n## Examples\\n\\n❌ \\"This EmailValidator class might be more complex than necessary, have you\\nconsidered whether all these validation rules are needed at this stage?\\"\\n\\n✅ \`L12-38: reuse: duplicated input validator. Reuse the established parser without weakening accepted-input validation.\`\\n\\n✅ \`L4: native: moment.js imported for one format call. Intl.DateTimeFormat, 0 deps.\`\\n\\n✅ \`L18-29: reuse: slugify helper duplicates src/lib/slug.ts slugify. Delete it, import the existing one.\`\\n\\n✅ \`repo.py:L88: yagni: AbstractRepository with one implementation. Inline it until a second one exists.\`\\n\\n✅ \`L52-71: delete: retry wrapper around an idempotent local call. Nothing replaces it.\`\\n\\n✅ \`L30-44: shrink: manual loop builds dict. dict(zip(keys, values)), 1 line.\`\\n\\n## Scoring\\n\\nEnd with the only metric that matters: \`net: -<N> lines possible.\`\\n\\nIf there is nothing to cut, say \`No supported simplification found.\` and stop. This is not a correctness or release approval.\\n\\n## Boundaries\\n\\nScope: over-engineering and complexity only. Correctness bugs, security holes, and performance are explicitly out of scope. Route them to a normal review pass, not this one. Required repository coverage is not bloat: preserve unit, real-composition, snapshot, security, and lifecycle tests rather than treating one smoke check as sufficient. Does not apply the fixes, only lists them. \\"stop ponytail-review\\" or \\"normal mode\\": revert to verbose review style.\\n</skill_instructions>\\n</skill_content>"}],"isError":false}],"role":"user","id":"{{sessionId}}"}},"sourceEventSeqs":[38],"surfaceOp":"append"}
